   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Typed Split Wipe\n\nA centered cursorless type build exits through opposing fixed-layout glyph wipes.\n\nCategory: typography. Length: 2.5 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- A product or feature introduction should type itself cleanly before breaking into controlled directional fragments.\n- One short anchor must stay visible while the surrounding words are erased independently.\n\nAvoid when:\n- You need a conventional typewriter with a blinking caret and no exit: use typewriter.\n- Every character should rise or move independently: use per-character-rise.\n\nVariables:\n- prefix (string): Prefix, default \"Introducing\"\n- anchor (string): Anchor, default \"Nova\"\n- suffix (string): Suffix, default \"Smart Notes\"\n- type_frames (number, 6-60): Type frames, default 30\n- exit_at (number, 20-90): Exit at, default 50\n- exit_frames (number, 6-40): Exit frames, default 20\n- word_stagger (number, 0-12): Word stagger, default 4\n- anchor_shift (number, -200-0): Anchor shift, default -72\n- font_size (number, 12-120): Font size, default 42\n- color (color): Color, default \"#e8e8e8\"\n- font_weight (enum): Font weight, default \"400\"\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
  {
   "path": "scene.html",
   "role": "source",
   "content": "<!doctype html>\n<!--\n  Typed Split Wipe\n\n  A centered cursorless type build exits through opposing fixed-layout glyph wipes.\n\n  Ported to an HTML + GSAP sub-composition by usemosio/blocks from:\n  https://github.com/Remocn/remocn/blob/126221ae00ba86eb40b65731b125ff398687d3b7/registry/remocn/typed-split-wipe/index.tsx\n\n  MIT License\n\n  Copyright (c) 2026 Remocn\n\n  Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\n  of this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal\n  in the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights\n  to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell\n  copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is\n  furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n\n  The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all\n  copies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\n  THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR\n  IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\n  FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE\n  AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER\n  LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,\n  OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE\n  SOFTWARE.\n-->\n<html\n  lang=\"en\"\n  data-composition-id=\"typed-split-wipe\"\n  data-composition-duration=\"2.5\"\n  data-composition-variables='[\n    { \"id\": \"prefix\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Prefix\", \"description\": \"Words typed before the anchor. It wipes out to the left.\", \"default\": \"Introducing\" },\n    { \"id\": \"anchor\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Anchor\", \"description\": \"Short word that stays visible while the rest is erased.\", \"default\": \"Nova\" },\n    { \"id\": \"suffix\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Suffix\", \"description\": \"Words typed after the anchor. They wipe out one by one.\", \"default\": \"Smart Notes\" },\n    { \"id\": \"type_frames\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Type frames\", \"description\": \"Frames the typing takes (30 fps).\", \"default\": 30, \"min\": 6, \"max\": 60, \"step\": 1, \"unit\": \"frames\" },\n    { \"id\": \"exit_at\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Exit at\", \"description\": \"Frame where the wipes start.\", \"default\": 50, \"min\": 20, \"max\": 90, \"step\": 1, \"unit\": \"frames\" },\n    { \"id\": \"exit_frames\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Exit frames\", \"description\": \"Frames the exit takes.\", \"default\": 20, \"min\": 6, \"max\": 40, \"step\": 1, \"unit\": \"frames\" },\n    { \"id\": \"word_stagger\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Word stagger\", \"description\": \"Frames between each suffix word wiping out.\", \"default\": 4, \"min\": 0, \"max\": 12, \"step\": 1, \"unit\": \"frames\" },\n    { \"id\": \"anchor_shift\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Anchor shift\", \"description\": \"Pixels the anchor slides left at 42 px type, as the prefix wipes away.\", \"default\": -72, \"min\": -200, \"max\": 0, \"step\": 1, \"unit\": \"px\" },\n    { \"id\": \"font_size\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Font size\", \"description\": \"Type size in pixels. Longer text shrinks to fit the frame.\", \"default\": 42, \"min\": 12, \"max\": 120, \"step\": 1, \"unit\": \"px\" },\n    { \"id\": \"color\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Color\", \"description\": \"Text color.\", \"default\": \"#e8e8e8\" },\n    { \"id\": \"font_weight\", \"type\": \"enum\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Font weight\", \"description\": \"Weight of the text.\", \"default\": \"400\", \"options\": [{\"value\": \"400\", \"label\": \"Regular\"}, {\"value\": \"500\", \"label\": \"Medium\"}, {\"value\": \"600\", \"label\": \"Semibold\"}, {\"value\": \"700\", \"label\": \"Bold\"}] }\n  ]'\n>\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <title>Typed Split Wipe</title>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <template>\n      <link\n        rel=\"stylesheet\"\n        href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Geist:wght@400;500;600;700&amp;display=block\"\n      />\n      <style>\n        #root {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n          overflow: hidden;\n          container-type: size;\n          color: var(--color, #e8e8e8);\n          font-family: var(--font-display, Geist, system-ui, sans-serif);\n          pointer-events: none;\n        }\n        .tsw-stage {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n          display: flex;\n          align-items: center;\n          justify-content: center;\n        }\n        .tsw-text { letter-spacing: -0.03em; line-height: 1; white-space: pre; }\n        .tsw-split { display: none; align-items: baseline; gap: 0.25em; }\n        .tsw-part { display: inline-block; }\n      </style>\n\n      <div id=\"root\" data-composition-id=\"typed-split-wipe\" data-duration=\"2.5\" data-fps=\"30\">\n        <div id=\"tsw-clip\" class=\"tsw-stage clip\" data-start=\"0\" data-duration=\"2.5\" data-track-index=\"0\">\n          <span id=\"tsw-typed\" class=\"tsw-text\"></span>\n          <span id=\"tsw-split\" class=\"tsw-text tsw-split\"></span>\n        </div>\n\n        <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.14.2/dist/gsap.min.js\"></script>\n        <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.14.2/dist/CustomEase.min.js\"></script>\n        <script>\n          (function () {\n            \"use strict\";\n            var root = document.getElementById(\"root\");\n            var vars =\n              window.__hyperframes && window.__hyperframes.getVariables\n                ? window.__hyperframes.getVariables()\n                : {};\n            function num(value, fallback, min, max) {\n              var n = Number(value);\n              return Number.isFinite(n) ? Math.min(max, Math.max(min, n)) : fallback;\n            }\n            function str(value, fallback) {\n              return typeof value === \"string\" && value.trim() ? value : fallback;\n            }\n            function pick(value, list, fallback) {\n              return list.indexOf(String(value)) >= 0 ? String(value) : fallback;\n            }\n            gsap.registerPlugin(CustomEase);\n            function bz(id, a, b, c, d) {\n              return CustomEase.create(\"tsw-\" + id, \"M0,0 C\" + a + \",\" + b + \" \" + c + \",\" + d + \" 1,1\");\n            }\n            // interpolate(frame, [a, b], [from, to], { easing }) as a tween (frames at 30 fps).\n            function tw(tl, el, from, to, a, b, ease, keep) {\n              var t = Object.assign({}, to, { duration: (b - a) / 30, ease: ease || \"none\", immediateRender: !keep });\n              tl.fromTo(el, from, t, a / 30);\n            }\n            // Shrink an element's font size so it fits a fraction of the frame width.\n            function fit(el, size, frac) {\n              el.style.fontSize = size + \"px\";\n              var maxWidth = Math.max(1, root.clientWidth * frac);\n              if (el.scrollWidth > maxWidth) {\n                size = Math.max(12, size * (maxWidth / el.scrollWidth));\n                el.style.fontSize = size + \"px\";\n              }\n              return size;\n            }\n            var TOTAL = parseFloat(root.dataset.duration || \"2.5\");\n            function finish(tl) {\n              if (tl.duration() < TOTAL) tl.to({}, { duration: TOTAL - tl.duration() });\n              tl.seek(0);\n              window.__timelines = window.__timelines || {};\n              window.__timelines[\"typed-split-wipe\"] = tl;\n            }\n            // interpolate() with clamping, easing given as a function of progress.\n            function ip(f, a, b, from, to, ease) {\n              var p = b === a ? 1 : Math.min(1, Math.max(0, (f - a) / (b - a)));\n              return from + (to - from) * (ease ? ease(p) : p);\n            }\n            var prefix = typeof vars.prefix === \"string\" ? vars.prefix : \"Introducing\";\n            var anchor = typeof vars.anchor === \"string\" ? vars.anchor : \"Nova\";\n            var suffix = typeof vars.suffix === \"string\" ? vars.suffix : \"Smart Notes\";\n            var weight = pick(vars.font_weight, [\"400\", \"500\", \"600\", \"700\"], \"400\");\n            if (typeof vars.color === \"string\" && vars.color) root.style.setProperty(\"--color\", vars.color);\n            var typeFrames = num(vars.type_frames, 30, 6, 60);\n            var exitAt = num(vars.exit_at, 50, 20, 90);\n            var exitFrames = num(vars.exit_frames, 20, 6, 40);\n            var wordStagger = num(vars.word_stagger, 4, 0, 12);\n            var anchorShift = num(vars.anchor_shift, -72, -200, 0);\n            var typed = document.getElementById(\"tsw-typed\");\n            var split = document.getElementById(\"tsw-split\");\n            var fullText = [prefix, anchor, suffix].filter(Boolean).join(\" \");\n            var chars = Array.from(fullText);\n            typed.textContent = fullText;\n            typed.style.fontWeight = weight;\n            split.style.fontWeight = weight;\n            var size = fit(typed, num(vars.font_size, 42, 12, 120), 0.9);\n            split.style.fontSize = size + \"px\";\n            typed.textContent = \"\";\n            var k = size / 42;\n\n            var inout = bz(\"wipe\", 0.455, 0.03, 0.515, 0.955);\n            var partPrefix = null, partAnchor = null, words = [];\n            if (prefix) { partPrefix = document.createElement(\"span\"); partPrefix.className = \"tsw-part\"; partPrefix.textContent = prefix; split.appendChild(partPrefix); }\n            if (anchor) { partAnchor = document.createElement(\"span\"); partAnchor.className = \"tsw-part\"; partAnchor.textContent = anchor; split.appendChild(partAnchor); }\n            suffix.trim().split(/\\s+/).filter(Boolean).forEach(function (w, i) {\n              var s = document.createElement(\"span\");\n              s.className = \"tsw-part\";\n              s.id = \"tsw-word-\" + i;\n              s.textContent = w;\n              split.appendChild(s);\n              words.push(s);\n            });\n            var P = { f: 0 };\n            function apply() {\n              var f = P.f;\n              if (f < exitAt) {\n                var tp = ip(f, 0, Math.max(typeFrames, 0.001), 0, chars.length);\n                var n = Math.min(chars.length, Math.max(1, Math.floor(tp) + 1));\n                typed.textContent = chars.slice(0, n).join(\"\");\n                typed.style.display = \"inline\";\n                split.style.display = \"none\";\n                return;\n              }\n              typed.style.display = \"none\";\n              split.style.display = \"inline-flex\";\n              var pe = ip(f, exitAt, exitAt + exitFrames, 0, 1, inout);\n              var as = exitAt + Math.max(exitFrames - 6, 0);\n              var ae = ip(f, as, as + 6, 0, 1, inout);\n              if (partPrefix) partPrefix.style.clipPath = \"inset(0 \" + pe * 100 + \"% 0 0)\";\n              if (partAnchor) {\n                partAnchor.style.clipPath = \"inset(0 \" + ae * 50 + \"% 0 \" + ae * 50 + \"%)\";\n                partAnchor.style.transform = \"translateX(\" + anchorShift * k * pe + \"px)\";\n              }\n              words.forEach(function (w, i) {\n                var st = exitAt + 2 + i * wordStagger;\n                w.style.clipPath = \"inset(0 0 0 \" + ip(f, st, st + exitFrames * 0.65, 0, 1, inout) * 100 + \"%)\";\n              });\n            }\n            apply();\n            var tl = gsap.timeline({ paused: true });\n            tl.to(P, { f: TOTAL * 30, duration: TOTAL, ease: \"none\", onUpdate: apply }, 0);\n            finish(tl);\n          })();\n        </script>\n      </div>\n    </template>\n  </body>\n</html>\n"
  }
 ],
